text:
maria: Quick report from today's onboarding run: sample-app printed a full Python traceback when the token refresh endpoint returned 401 -> users got confused and filed support tickets. We should standardize the SDK error surfaces so UIs can map to friendly copy.

sam: Agreed. Current state across SDKs is inconsistent. I sketched a small taxonomy: ClientError (4xx except auth/rate), AuthError (401/403), RateLimitError (429), ServerError (5xx). Each error should expose `error_code` and `http_status`.

jordan: +1 to taxonomy. One thing: 429 is tricky for our customers. Sometimes it's transient (burst) and sometimes it's steady-limit. We should include a boolean `is_retryable` and a numeric `ttl_retry` (seconds) when header present.

lee: Naming bikeshed: `error_code` vs `code`. I prefer `error_code` to avoid collisions with other metadata keys in apps. Also propose `user_recovery` with recommended consumer action, e.g. `re-auth`, `wait`, `contact-support`.

alex: Example minimal JSON payload proposal (server -> client): ```json
{
  "error_code": "auth.token_expired",
  "http_status": 401,
  "message": "API token expired",
  "user_recovery": "re-auth",
  "docs_link": "https://docs.redwood.ai/errors#auth.token_expired"
}
```

maria: Nice. For rate limit: ```json
{
  "error_code": "rate.limit",
  "http_status": 429,
  "message": "Rate limit exceeded",
  "is_retryable": true,
  "ttl_retry": 10,
  "user_recovery": "wait",
  "docs_link": "https://docs.redwood.ai/errors#rate.limit"
}
```

sam: Implementation plan: 1) add server-side header + JSON body for all error responses, 2) SDKs parse body and raise typed exceptions that subclass from a common base (e.g., `RedwoodError`), 3) keep backward-compatible behavior by mapping to existing exceptions when body absent.

jordan: SDK spec detail: typed classes should be named `RedwoodAuthError`, `RedwoodRateLimitError`, `RedwoodClientError`, `RedwoodServerError`. Each should expose properties: `error_code` (str), `http_status` (int), `ttl_retry` (int|None), `user_recovery` (str|None), `raw_body` (dict|None).

lee: Quick sample snippets for handling in apps. Go: ```go
resp, err := client.Generate(ctx, req)
if err != nil {
  if re, ok := err.(redwood.RateLimitError); ok {
    wait := time.Second * time.Duration(re.TTLRetryOrDefault(1))
    time.Sleep(wait)
    retry()
  } else if _, ok := err.(redwood.AuthError); ok {
    triggerReauthFlow()
  } else {
    log.Printf("unexpected error: %v", err)
  }
}
```

alex: JS sample (browser): ```js
try {
  await client.generate(opts)
} catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof RedwoodRateLimitError) {
    showToast(`Rate limited. Try again in ${e.ttl_retry || 1}s`)
  } else if (e instanceof RedwoodAuthError) {
    promptLogin()
  } else {
    console.error(e)
    if (window.__REDWOOD_DEBUG__) showModal(e.raw_body || e.message)
  }
}
```

maria: Operational asks: update sample-app to catch these types and surface friendly copy by default (with a developer toggle for raw debug). Add a short migration note in release notes indicating `RuntimeError` catch-alls may no longer see typed attributes.

sam: CI: I'll add tests to sample-apps repo that mock 401 and 429 bodies and assert the app shows the expected friendly string and that SDKs expose typed classes. We'll gate the SDK PRs with these tests.

jordan: Two edge cases to call out: 1) older clients that don't parse JSON bodies (we should fallback to headers), 2) network-level 502/504 where retry policies should be determined by client config, not server body. Document both.

ci-bot: CI: sample-apps/error-handling-tests passed on branch error-surface (build #921) :white_check_mark:

lee: I'll open the RFC with the proposed JSON keys and the mapping table for HTTP -> typed error. Draft ETA: tomorrow morning. Assign owners: lee (RFC), sam (sample-app CI tests), maria (sample-app UI changes).

alex: Tiny naming nit: prefer `ttl_retry` over `retry_after` to emphasize it's advisory, not authoritative.

maria: Works for me. One more ask: include copy snippets for common cases (auth, rate, server) so support can paste into replies.

sam: Adding to checklist. Closing loop: once RFC merges we'll cut SDK PRs with changelog entries.

jordan: Thanks all — nice incremental plan. :rocket:
